<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs-Tuesday est 110,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs-Tuesday est 110,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interior Iowa-southern Minnesota hog receipts estimate for Tuesday was 110000 vs wk ago 113000, yr ago 99000</p>
<p>Estimates include generally about 60 percent Carcass Base Hogs.</p>
<p>Barrows and gilts 1.00-1.50 lower compared to mid-session Monday. Trade slow to moderate for light demand moderate to heavy offerings.</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>			     Country		    Plants</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    54.50 -55.50	   55.50 -56.50</p>
<p>few			54.00 -56.00	   55.00  57.00</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs	    52.50 -55.50	   53.00 -56.50</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>280-300 lbs	    49.00 -54.00	   49.50 -55.00</p>
<p>Sows: 450 lbs up steady to 1.00 higher, 450 dn steady to 1.00</p>
<p>lower.</p>
<p>US 1-3  300-450 lbs. 43.00 -44.00	   43.00 -45.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.	   46.00 -47.00	   46.00 -48.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	    47.00 -51.00	   47.00 -52.00</p>
<p>Note: Prices quoted represent sales of hogs averaging 73-74 pct. carcass yields with mostly 1.00-1.25 inches of last rib backfat and 47-48 pct. lean.</p>
<p>Special considerations and grade premiums not reflected in base prices.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
